  "pli-tv-kd5:13.7.1": "“Robe-cloth” renders <i lang='pi' translate='no'>cīvara</i>. See Appendix of Technical Terms. ",
  "pli-tv-kd5:13.7.2": "To clarify, the issue at stake is people giving cloth at a monastery for a monk who is away. The monk does not know he has been given cloth until he returns to the monastery. ",
  "pli-tv-kd5:13.7.3": "",
  "pli-tv-kd5:13.7.4": "",
  "pli-tv-kd5:13.7.5": "This refers to <a href='https://suttacentral.net/pli-tv-bu-vb-np1/en/brahmali#2.17.1'>Bu Np 1:2.17.1</a>/Bi Np 13, which prohibits a monk from keeping extra robe cloth for more than ten days. The point made here is that these monks would count the days from the moment the cloth was given. If they arrived at the monastery more than ten days after the cloth had been given, they would not be able to receive it without falling into an offense. ",
  "pli-tv-kd5:13.7.6": "",
  "pli-tv-kd5:13.7.7": "",
